# Every product on this box drops its own <name>-site.caddy here and it is
# picked up automatically. The entrypoint writes phoenix-feed-site.caddy;
# VistaScan's API, which shares this droplet, supplies vistascan-site.caddy.
#
# A glob rather than one literal import per product, for two reasons.
#
# The route used to be added by editing this file directly on the server, so it
# lived as an uncommitted modification that any `git pull --ff-only` or
# `git checkout` would silently drop, taking VistaScan's only public route with
# it.
#
# More importantly, a literal import of a missing file is a hard adapter error,
# not a warning, and this container's /tmp does not survive recreation. A
# recreate would therefore leave Caddy unable to start at all, taking down
# cactuswatch.com as collateral for a neighbour's missing file. A glob that
# matches nothing logs a warning and carries on, so the worst case is the
# missing site 404ing while everything else stays up.
import /tmp/*-site.caddy
